WEBVTT

00:02.835 --> 00:05.165
Shinjitai
I want to believe

00:05.265 --> 00:08.325
ano hi mitsuketa hikari
In the light that I found that day

00:08.805 --> 00:11.545
kimi to kawashita
Because I still have

00:11.545 --> 00:16.205
tatta hitotsuno yakusoku ga arukara
That one promise that I made to you

00:16.615 --> 00:23.605
mou tachidomarazuni aruite yukitai
I want to keep walking, never stopping

00:25.325 --> 00:28.195
Dragon Drive

00:28.195 --> 00:33.715
uresugita kajitsu wo kajiru youni
Like biting into an overripe fruit

00:33.825 --> 00:36.795
yowai jibun ni
I was spoiling myself

00:36.795 --> 00:40.065
amaetsuzukete ita
I was giving in to my weakness

00:40.535 --> 00:44.905
kimi ni deawanakereba
If I hadn't met you

00:44.905 --> 00:46.875
ima mo
I'd still...

00:46.875 --> 00:53.215
kabe wo kowasu koto nado dekinakatta yo
...be unable to break the walls around me

00:54.915 --> 00:57.285
wasurenai
I'll never forget

00:57.285 --> 01:00.515
ano hi kanjita itami
The pain that I felt that day

01:00.825 --> 01:05.825
nido to ano basho modoritakunai
I never want to go back to that place

01:05.825 --> 01:07.425
motto tsuyoku
This strong feeling

01:07.525 --> 01:09.935
shinjitai
I want to believe

01:09.935 --> 01:13.095
ano hi mitsuketa hikari
In the light I found that day

01:13.465 --> 01:18.545
kakkowarui to warawaretemo ii
Let them laugh and call me a loser

01:18.545 --> 01:21.275
bukiyou dakara
Because I'm clumsy

01:21.275 --> 01:28.975
onaji ikikata shika erabenainda
I can only choose to live life this way

01:50.675 --> 01:52.005
Somebody...

01:53.045 --> 01:54.665
...please save me!

02:01.515 --> 02:03.015
It was just a dream.

02:03.015 --> 02:05.145
That same dream again.

02:07.225 --> 02:10.085
What in the world's going on?

02:14.095 --> 02:15.585
I'm totally late!

02:17.195 --> 02:19.325
Oh, well.

02:19.905 --> 02:21.335
A little more sleep can't hurt.

02:21.575 --> 02:23.775
Even if I leave right now...

02:23.775 --> 02:25.675
...I'll still be late.

02:27.105 --> 02:30.675
The Sleeping Dragon

02:33.315 --> 02:35.515
Reiji's late again today.

02:36.315 --> 02:38.115
What is he thinking?!

02:39.185 --> 02:40.055
Please!

02:40.055 --> 02:43.615
With you on our team, we'd breeze
through the regional preliminaries!

02:44.795 --> 02:47.125
At least for the regional preliminary round?

02:48.535 --> 02:50.435
I just can't get myself excited about it.

02:50.835 --> 02:52.865
But I'll think about it.

02:52.865 --> 02:54.475
I'm counting on you, Kyoji!

02:54.475 --> 02:56.565
Yeah, he'll think about it!

02:57.105 --> 02:58.945
Today, it's the basketball team.

02:58.945 --> 03:01.635
You're being canvassed
by a different team every day.

03:02.245 --> 03:03.675
You're awesome!

03:04.375 --> 03:08.405
Well, I guess it comes naturally
when you're perfect at whatever you do.

03:08.885 --> 03:09.875
Yes.

03:10.215 --> 03:11.425
I am perfect at everything.

03:11.425 --> 03:13.325
That's my motto.

03:14.325 --> 03:16.185
U-Um, Kyoji?

03:17.865 --> 03:19.325
Please read this!

03:20.265 --> 03:22.565
Thank you. I'll read it with pleasure.

03:26.765 --> 03:29.005
And to top it off, you're popular with girls.

03:29.005 --> 03:31.195
You're disgusting.

03:32.305 --> 03:34.295
Just write her some sorta reply.

03:35.815 --> 03:37.305
C-Come on!

03:42.615 --> 03:45.055
I might've slept too much.

03:45.055 --> 03:46.315
My head hurts.

03:52.025 --> 03:53.395
Hey, that's dangerous!

04:07.275 --> 04:08.835
What did you do that for?!

04:09.645 --> 04:13.205
Wait, aren't you the King of Tardiness
from Class B?!

04:13.815 --> 04:15.685
Hey, isn't that Reiji?

04:16.155 --> 04:17.205
About time!

04:17.255 --> 04:19.315
Oh, no. He's being hassled.

04:19.725 --> 04:22.415
The other guy's Daisuke Hagiwara
from Class A.

04:22.655 --> 04:26.285
He thinks he's so great,
being around Kyoji all the time.

04:26.565 --> 04:28.555
I feel sorry for Reiji.

04:30.835 --> 04:33.565
I've been apologizing over and over again.

04:33.565 --> 04:34.505
I'm sorry.

04:34.975 --> 04:39.335
Hey, if a simple apology solved everything,
we wouldn't need police or judge of hell!

04:39.975 --> 04:41.215
Th-Then what...

04:41.215 --> 04:42.805
This is the answer!

04:43.575 --> 04:44.735
Stop it!

04:46.945 --> 04:47.935
Maiko.

04:51.325 --> 04:53.555
M-Maiko Yukino?!

04:53.825 --> 04:56.495
M-My sweet honey!

04:56.495 --> 04:57.825
Stop it, already!

04:57.825 --> 05:00.565
You're in junior high,
so grow up and stop picking on the weak!

05:00.565 --> 05:04.125
If you insist on continuing,
I'll be your opponent!

05:05.305 --> 05:06.495
S-S-S...

05:07.705 --> 05:08.865
Sorry.

05:11.645 --> 05:13.765
That's fine, as long as you understand.

05:14.445 --> 05:16.305
How pathetic!

05:16.615 --> 05:18.845
If I hadn't jumped in to help!

05:19.145 --> 05:22.185
I don't remember asking
you to jump in and help.

05:22.185 --> 05:23.755
Don't talk back!

05:23.755 --> 05:26.415
Also, I hear that you quit your
extracurricular club again.

05:27.425 --> 05:28.395
Yeah.

05:28.395 --> 05:30.445
You didn't even last three days!

05:30.795 --> 05:33.925
First the baseball team, then the soccer
team and now the comic book study club!

05:34.265 --> 05:36.785
You showed up a few times
and quit each one!

05:37.065 --> 05:41.205
You know, I just don't think
I'm suited for that stuff.

05:41.205 --> 05:44.335
- How can I explain it?
- And then there's this!

05:44.335 --> 05:46.065
Reiji: 27 percent

05:46.745 --> 05:48.575
M-My test paper!

05:49.215 --> 05:52.205
You get grades like this because
you're always late to school!

05:52.345 --> 05:56.075
Everyone thinks you only come to school
for the free lunch.

05:57.485 --> 05:59.785
Seriously, at this rate,
you'll hafta repeat a grade!

05:59.785 --> 06:00.985
Repeat a grade?

06:00.985 --> 06:02.755
That may not be good.

06:03.925 --> 06:06.155
A week's worth of notes from class.

06:06.295 --> 06:08.595
I've marked areas likely to be on the test.

06:08.795 --> 06:10.285
M-Maiko!

06:10.395 --> 06:11.905
Y-You're letting me copy your notes?!

06:11.905 --> 06:12.935
Sure!

06:12.935 --> 06:16.905
But in return, you'll go everywhere
with me for the rest of the day!

06:16.905 --> 06:17.775
No.

06:17.775 --> 06:18.845
What?!

06:18.845 --> 06:22.745
Since we've been kids, the worst things
happen when I hang around you!

06:23.175 --> 06:24.985
You made me investigate the sewers...

06:24.985 --> 06:27.975
...and then we got lost in the mountains,
looking for a phantom snake.

06:28.285 --> 06:29.345
I see.

06:29.585 --> 06:31.085
Hey, everyone, look here!

06:31.085 --> 06:32.655
It's Reiji Ozora's test! His test!

06:32.655 --> 06:34.185
No, stop that! Wait!

06:34.185 --> 06:35.955
Okay, okay, you win!

06:35.955 --> 06:37.225
I win what?!

06:37.225 --> 06:38.455
I'll go with you wherever you wish!

06:38.725 --> 06:41.215
That's it, right? I just have to go with you?

06:42.535 --> 06:43.585
Exactly.

06:43.895 --> 06:45.895
What? A game?!

06:45.935 --> 06:46.665
Right!

06:46.665 --> 06:49.505
You know, you give up too easily
whatever you do, Reiji.

06:50.035 --> 06:50.935
Do I?

06:50.935 --> 06:54.935
But a friend introduced me
to an awesome game the other day!

06:55.375 --> 06:56.745
An awesome game?

06:56.745 --> 07:01.235
Yeah, and I think if you tried that game,
even you would really get into it, Reiji!

07:01.285 --> 07:04.415
Come to think of it, there was a time
when I was into that sort of stuff.

07:04.785 --> 07:06.915
But this isn't just any old game!

07:07.355 --> 07:09.225
You'll understand when you see it!

07:09.225 --> 07:10.195
Hurry, hurry!

07:11.625 --> 07:12.885
I wonder.

07:14.735 --> 07:16.225
This place, here! Hurry!

07:17.295 --> 07:19.825
What's with this rundown cheap candy store?

07:20.135 --> 07:22.035
Can't you read the sign above?

07:22.035 --> 07:24.265
Ryugujo: The Sea Palace
Ryu-gu-jo?

07:24.435 --> 07:26.105
Right! Here we go, Mr. Turtle!

07:29.345 --> 07:30.915
Come on, this way!

07:30.915 --> 07:31.945
H-Hey!

07:31.945 --> 07:33.575
You can't just walk into someone's home!

07:33.685 --> 07:35.185
Especially with muddy shoes!

07:35.185 --> 07:37.655
It's okay, we're going in here!

07:37.655 --> 07:39.085
Huh?! Going in where?!

07:41.125 --> 07:42.985
Press this, and?

07:46.865 --> 07:49.335
The closet's an elevator?

07:49.435 --> 07:52.165
Two people on our way to the Ryugujo!

07:55.335 --> 07:57.735
What in the world?

08:05.315 --> 08:07.175
What is this?

08:10.915 --> 08:14.585
How... How could something like this
exist beneath a cheap candy store?

08:15.825 --> 08:17.125
What's going on?

08:19.225 --> 08:20.325
Wh-What was that?

08:20.325 --> 08:23.235
They're showing the current match
on the monitor!

08:23.235 --> 08:25.255
- Come with me!
- R-Right.

08:29.135 --> 08:30.735
Go!

08:30.735 --> 08:34.505
- Way to go!
- Good move!

08:34.505 --> 08:38.575
Well? This is the game
I was talking about.

08:39.185 --> 08:40.585
It's called Dragon Drive!

08:41.145 --> 08:43.915
Dragon... Drive?

08:43.985 --> 08:45.545
This is a game?

08:46.325 --> 08:48.115
No, I swear it looks like...

08:48.595 --> 08:50.315
...like this is actually happening!

08:52.895 --> 08:54.795
You'll see for yourself once you try it, Reiji.

08:54.995 --> 08:58.365
That image onscreen
is one hundred percent virtual reality!

08:58.735 --> 09:01.205
You ride a dragon
that looks like the real thing...

09:01.205 --> 09:04.105
...and battle in a city that's like a real city,
all as part of the game!

09:04.205 --> 09:05.905
I'll see once I try it?

09:06.075 --> 09:08.065
Can I play this game, too?

09:09.115 --> 09:10.235
Beginning to feel excited?

09:10.945 --> 09:12.745
A-A little bit.

09:12.745 --> 09:13.575
That's plenty!

09:13.745 --> 09:15.945
Okay, then let's go and get you registered!

09:17.855 --> 09:20.025
W-Wait, I don't feel ready for it yet!

09:20.025 --> 09:21.515
Never mind that!

09:22.555 --> 09:24.585
My sweet honey!

09:24.695 --> 09:26.525
Maiko Yukino!

09:27.625 --> 09:30.395
That guy. It's that guy again!

09:30.565 --> 09:33.195
What is he to her, anyway?!

09:33.865 --> 09:36.535
Sorry for the wait, Mr. Reiji Ozora.

09:36.535 --> 09:38.475
Enjoy the game!

09:38.475 --> 09:40.075
- I get a cell phone?!
- Yes.

09:40.075 --> 09:43.875
All you do now is insert the dragon card
you selected into the cell phone...

09:43.875 --> 09:47.075
...and a dragon belonging only to you
will appear in the virtual world.

09:47.585 --> 09:49.645
My own dragon?

09:49.915 --> 09:52.155
Yes, the dragon used in the game...

09:52.155 --> 09:55.395
...is selected by converting our physical
abilities with a digital genome code.

09:55.395 --> 09:57.855
That's how they match you up
with your perfect dragon!

09:58.095 --> 10:01.325
My own... dragon?

10:01.595 --> 10:04.435
Now, everyone,
direct your attention to the monitor!

10:04.435 --> 10:06.425
Sasaki's Dragon is...

10:07.365 --> 10:09.335
Arateno Hydra!

10:09.505 --> 10:10.475
Wow!

10:10.475 --> 10:12.145
That's a type of dragon we see a lot of.

10:12.145 --> 10:14.575
Every once in a while, a kid will
introduce an incredible dragon.

10:14.575 --> 10:17.235
I-I'll have a great big dragon like that?

10:17.675 --> 10:18.665
Reiji!

10:19.515 --> 10:20.845
Wh-What is it?!

10:20.845 --> 10:23.885
Reiji, you've never been good
at anything until now!

10:23.885 --> 10:25.355
Guilty as charged!

10:25.355 --> 10:27.185
This is why I believe in you!

10:27.785 --> 10:31.955
Reiji, I believe there is a sleeping dragon
deep inside you waiting to be awakened.

10:33.165 --> 10:34.665
A sleeping dragon?!

10:34.665 --> 10:39.135
Y-You're saying there's
an unknown power within me?

10:39.135 --> 10:40.965
Cool!

10:42.375 --> 10:45.645
Boy, he's got his heart set
on introducing some incredible dragon.

10:45.645 --> 10:47.305
I didn't know he was so easy to manipulate.

10:47.505 --> 10:50.065
Now, for our next participant! Let's do it!

10:50.475 --> 10:52.815
Welcome, Reiji Ozora!

10:53.915 --> 10:55.045
Ah? Um, yeah.

10:56.515 --> 11:00.355
Just leave everything to me, Miss L,
while I access the dragon data!

11:01.025 --> 11:04.015
I'll find the one dragon
that's perfectly suited for you!

11:04.155 --> 11:06.255
Without further ado... Access, start!

11:09.365 --> 11:11.035
Wh-What's this sound?!

11:11.035 --> 11:15.335
Will the dragon sleeping within me
really wake up to something like this?

11:17.005 --> 11:18.935
Awaken, my dragon!

11:24.145 --> 11:26.385
Now, we have the results!

11:26.385 --> 11:28.175
Reiji Ozora's dragon is...

11:28.755 --> 11:29.715
This one!

11:37.225 --> 11:38.195
All right!

11:38.425 --> 11:39.415
Wha?!

11:39.595 --> 11:42.685
Th-This is the dragon sleeping within me?

11:46.705 --> 11:48.865
I-It really is sleeping!

12:04.115 --> 12:06.285
Wh-What could this be?!

12:06.285 --> 12:08.345
Its name and characteristics are unknown!

12:08.495 --> 12:11.825
And among all dragons
currently registered...

12:11.825 --> 12:13.655
...it ranks the lowest in power by far!

12:15.365 --> 12:18.025
I was a fool to even have
a glimmer of hope.

12:20.305 --> 12:21.805
Okay, I win!

12:21.805 --> 12:24.205
I'll easily finish off that wimpy dragon!

12:24.205 --> 12:27.365
And then I'll be able to grasp
Maiko Yukino's heart!

12:29.715 --> 12:31.475
The parameter figures are awful.

12:31.475 --> 12:33.415
Battle power appears as zero.

12:33.785 --> 12:36.045
Did we input data for such a weak dragon?

12:36.485 --> 12:39.885
Well, maybe it'll get stronger
if brought up right!

12:40.885 --> 12:43.285
Here's your Dragon Drive card.

12:43.795 --> 12:46.555
You're free to name the
dragon whatever you wish.

12:47.925 --> 12:49.165
Boy.

12:49.165 --> 12:51.225
I sure looked uncool...

12:51.765 --> 12:52.435
Okay.

12:52.435 --> 12:53.735
Sorry to keep you waiting!

12:53.735 --> 12:55.505
This is where the real battle begins!

12:55.505 --> 12:57.175
Shall we begin our next game?

12:57.175 --> 12:58.665
Yeah!

12:58.705 --> 13:00.405
W-Wait a minute!

13:00.405 --> 13:01.305
"Next game"?

13:01.305 --> 13:03.445
You mean I gotta play with this dragon?!

13:03.445 --> 13:04.535
Of course!

13:05.785 --> 13:08.645
The rule says we've all gotta fight
with our own dragons!

13:08.855 --> 13:10.615
Stop complaining, and let's get started!

13:10.615 --> 13:13.315
Or are you afraid, Reiji Ozora?

13:14.485 --> 13:17.695
Easy for you to say...

13:17.695 --> 13:19.685
...but can this dragon really fight at all?

13:20.165 --> 13:21.465
Don't worry.

13:21.465 --> 13:23.725
If worse comes to worst, I'll back you up!

13:23.995 --> 13:25.465
What good will that do me?

13:25.465 --> 13:28.405
Okay! We'll quickly get started!

13:28.775 --> 13:31.765
Do you all remember
the Dragon Drive rules?

13:32.005 --> 13:34.545
It's a battle royale format
where anything and everything goes!

13:34.545 --> 13:37.235
And what's most important
is how you control your dragon!

13:37.545 --> 13:40.885
If you maintain a pure heart
and become one with your dragon...

13:40.885 --> 13:43.005
...you'll be able to control your dragon
however you wish!

13:43.155 --> 13:45.385
"B-Become one with my dragon"?

13:45.655 --> 13:48.625
Now, players, insert your cards
into your cell phones...

13:48.625 --> 13:51.025
...and secure your helmets!

13:59.165 --> 14:00.205
Now, then.

14:00.205 --> 14:02.195
Commencing Dragon Drive!

14:02.375 --> 14:04.365
D-Break!

14:12.785 --> 14:14.215
It's pitch black.

14:24.255 --> 14:25.355
A-A city?!

14:27.295 --> 14:29.385
Ouch!

14:29.935 --> 14:31.695
What was that?!

14:33.105 --> 14:34.395
Th-This guy...

14:35.065 --> 14:37.405
It's the dragon they were calling my partner.

14:38.775 --> 14:42.335
Which means this is really
a virtual reality world?

14:42.745 --> 14:44.345
You're kidding! Awesome!

14:44.345 --> 14:46.315
Everything feels so real!

14:46.645 --> 14:48.515
Condition green. All satisfactory!

14:48.515 --> 14:51.715
Player A has moved to D-Mode
without any problem.

14:53.055 --> 14:54.525
Hey, wake up! Hey!

14:54.525 --> 14:56.645
This won't be much of a game
unless you move!

14:56.955 --> 14:58.985
Hey! I'm telling you to wake up!

15:04.765 --> 15:07.895
You really seem like a dopey dragon,
you know that?

15:16.475 --> 15:18.345
What are you doing?

15:21.415 --> 15:23.445
S-Stop it! That tickles!

15:25.285 --> 15:27.225
What was that sound?

15:30.395 --> 15:31.855
Wh-Wh-Wha...

15:32.295 --> 15:33.925
What's that thing?!

15:35.595 --> 15:37.395
I am so lucky!

15:37.395 --> 15:40.365
I didn't expect my target to be so near.

15:40.765 --> 15:42.405
You've gotta be kidding!

15:42.405 --> 15:44.375
I've gotta fight this huge thing?!

15:46.445 --> 15:47.675
Impossible!

15:47.675 --> 15:49.335
Hey, you! Listen up!

15:50.115 --> 15:52.115
You're that guy from earlier!

15:52.115 --> 15:53.875
I'm gonna ask you up front!

15:55.045 --> 15:57.675
What's your relationship
to Maiko Yukino?!

15:58.315 --> 15:59.615
Childhood friends.

16:00.285 --> 16:02.825
D-Don't think you can get away
with just making stuff up!

16:02.825 --> 16:04.295
I know your type!

16:04.295 --> 16:08.835
A mindless dope like you
isn't worthy of Maiko Yukino!

16:08.835 --> 16:09.815
Kanper!

16:10.165 --> 16:12.065
Time to hunt 'em down!

16:15.035 --> 16:16.505
N-No fair!

16:16.505 --> 16:18.945
How do you expect me to fight
against something like that?!

16:18.945 --> 16:22.415
H-He's still over there!

16:22.415 --> 16:24.845
G-Gotta think of a name.

16:24.845 --> 16:26.675
Chibi! Chibisuke! That'll do!

16:27.085 --> 16:28.915
Over here! Run to where I am!

16:30.585 --> 16:31.515
You fool!

16:31.515 --> 16:34.955
There's no way a dragon would listen
to its trainers during the first game!

16:38.325 --> 16:39.225
It's useless!

16:40.395 --> 16:42.055
Don't act so scared!

16:42.695 --> 16:44.795
I'm just as scared as you are!

16:45.135 --> 16:47.125
Come on! What are you gonna do?!

16:52.605 --> 16:53.635
Oww!

16:56.815 --> 16:59.075
I'll show him!

16:59.545 --> 17:01.535
We're running! Come with me, Chibisuke!

17:03.085 --> 17:05.555
- How pathetic!
- That's so lame!

17:05.725 --> 17:07.155
Those moves they just made...

17:10.395 --> 17:12.195
They were in synch.

17:12.195 --> 17:13.315
Could it be?

17:15.695 --> 17:18.185
Where is he? Where'd Reiji go?!

17:18.965 --> 17:21.735
Gholaoh! We're gonna return!

17:26.705 --> 17:28.005
Hello!

17:28.005 --> 17:29.345
What's the matter, Reiji?!

17:29.345 --> 17:32.435
Maiko! Some strange guy's attacking me!

17:36.585 --> 17:38.075
Do something about this!

17:38.285 --> 17:39.775
Reiji! Run away from there!

17:40.055 --> 17:41.785
I already am!

17:42.425 --> 17:43.895
It won't be that easy!

17:43.895 --> 17:44.855
Kanper!

17:59.305 --> 18:00.505
I-It's impossible.

18:00.505 --> 18:02.165
We can't get away from it.

18:04.945 --> 18:05.935
Chibi.

18:06.385 --> 18:08.145
Are you attacking?!

18:10.455 --> 18:12.545
What's that poor excuse for an attack?!

18:13.025 --> 18:14.515
He was so frightened a moment ago.

18:15.255 --> 18:17.525
He doesn't wanna lose either.

18:17.925 --> 18:21.365
But all I was thinking about
was how to escape.

18:23.265 --> 18:24.525
You're right!

18:24.765 --> 18:26.465
We can't run away any longer!

18:26.465 --> 18:29.435
Let's do what we can
to sock him a good one!

18:31.505 --> 18:33.475
Take this!

18:33.545 --> 18:35.205
What are you guys doing?!

18:35.375 --> 18:39.215
Do you really think you can harm
Kanper doing something like that?!

18:39.715 --> 18:40.735
Get real!

18:46.525 --> 18:48.025
Ouch.

18:48.025 --> 18:50.515
I guess it is impossible!

18:52.225 --> 18:53.095
Hey, Chibisuke!

18:53.595 --> 18:54.625
Are those wings?

18:54.625 --> 18:56.495
Can you fly?

18:56.795 --> 18:58.195
If you can fly...

18:58.195 --> 19:00.065
If you fly, we may still be able to fight!

19:00.805 --> 19:02.995
But what do you need to do to fly?

19:03.175 --> 19:05.235
Game's almost over!

19:05.745 --> 19:07.405
Fly! Fly!

19:08.045 --> 19:09.135
Please fly!

19:09.375 --> 19:10.905
Say your prayers!

19:18.825 --> 19:19.855
I did it!

19:19.855 --> 19:21.915
Now Maiko Yukino will be my girlfriend!

19:23.925 --> 19:24.915
Wha?

19:26.565 --> 19:28.025
Wh... Wh...

19:28.225 --> 19:30.255
What?!

19:30.795 --> 19:32.035
Wow, it's flying!

19:32.035 --> 19:32.935
It grew wings!

19:33.135 --> 19:36.335
The dragon's wings are bigger!

19:36.335 --> 19:38.665
Did that boy cause those wings
to grow suddenly?

19:38.905 --> 19:41.275
The game's not programmed
to do anything of the sort.

19:41.805 --> 19:43.035
How can this be explained?

19:45.315 --> 19:46.475
Reiji!

19:46.915 --> 19:49.845
That ball of fire should hit
from this distance!

19:50.185 --> 19:51.875
Do it!

20:07.065 --> 20:09.055
I-I thought I'd die.

20:10.505 --> 20:12.445
What in the world was that?!

20:12.445 --> 20:16.375
Hey, s-stop it. You're tickling me.

20:23.385 --> 20:25.145
Daisuke, game over!

20:25.785 --> 20:27.155
What?

20:27.155 --> 20:30.095
But... But that's not possible!

20:32.495 --> 20:35.085
- A last-minute victory!
- It's a miracle!

20:35.595 --> 20:37.085
A miracle?

20:37.765 --> 20:38.735
No.

20:38.735 --> 20:41.995
Dragon Drive is not programmed
to allow miracles.

20:42.835 --> 20:44.305
Which would mean that kid is!

20:47.075 --> 20:49.065
This could be interesting.

20:52.015 --> 20:53.175
Reiji.

20:55.685 --> 20:57.715
Tell me, what happened back there?!

20:57.715 --> 20:59.945
How'd you do it? I can't believe it!

21:00.385 --> 21:03.955
The truth is, I can't exactly
explain what I did either.

21:03.955 --> 21:05.455
Huh? What do you mean?

21:05.455 --> 21:08.935
Just that, when I saw
this little guy trying to fight...

21:08.935 --> 21:11.555
...I felt that I should do something as well.

21:12.065 --> 21:15.295
I wasn't sure if it could fly
with such small wings.

21:15.535 --> 21:17.905
But then I felt this surge through my body...

21:17.905 --> 21:21.895
...and this little guy started flying
just as I envisioned it in my head!

21:22.275 --> 21:23.905
It was really thrilling!

21:25.275 --> 21:26.045
Huh?

21:26.045 --> 21:29.485
I guess maybe that's how it feels
to control a dragon.

21:29.815 --> 21:32.215
I think I could get excited about this game.

21:33.085 --> 21:34.985
Reiji Ozora.

21:35.185 --> 21:36.655
He could be an unexpected treasure.

21:37.655 --> 21:40.025
Cut it out, you're tickling me!

21:40.425 --> 21:43.095
It tickles!

21:43.095 --> 21:44.225
Stop it!

21:57.375 --> 22:00.115
Taikutsu datta
I was bored

22:00.115 --> 22:02.885
okubyou datta
I was a coward

22:02.885 --> 22:06.845
dareka wo jibun wo kizutsukete ita
I was hurting someone and myself

22:08.285 --> 22:11.055
tsuyogari itte
I tried to hide my weakness

22:11.055 --> 22:13.255
wagamama itte
I was being selfish

22:13.695 --> 22:17.825
doushiyoumonai kimochi mamoritsuzukete
Protecting the uncontrollable feeling

22:19.235 --> 22:21.905
otona ni natte
I became an adult

22:21.905 --> 22:24.635
kimi to deatte
Then I met you

22:24.635 --> 22:28.635
mune no sumikko yawarakaku natte
My heart got softened

22:29.945 --> 22:32.445
setsunaku natta
Longing for love

22:32.445 --> 22:35.445
dakishime atta
We embraced each other

22:35.445 --> 22:40.355
hakkiri mamorubeki mono wo mitsuketa
I finally knew what I wanted to protect

22:40.985 --> 22:43.725
tatta hitotsu no yuuki ga
Only one courage

22:43.725 --> 22:46.495
tatta hitotsu no kotoba ga
Just one word

22:46.495 --> 22:51.155
futari owaranai yume e to hakobu
Take us to an endless dream

22:51.865 --> 22:54.635
hon no chiisana yasashisa ga
Only a small kindness

22:54.635 --> 22:57.305
hon no wazuka na sasayaki ga
Only a small whisper

22:57.305 --> 23:01.965
futari wo sotto tsutsunde kureru
Wrap us gently

23:02.615 --> 23:07.135
zutto konomama asa ga kurumade
Until the morning comes

23:08.045 --> 23:13.745
zutto konomama asa ga kurumade
Until the morning comes

23:16.025 --> 23:18.825
Next Episode

23:20.395 --> 23:22.365
That last battle was a close call!

23:24.035 --> 23:25.765
I'll be in more danger the next time?

23:26.235 --> 23:28.425
What? I meet a new rival?

23:29.675 --> 23:32.335
I know! Maiko's in danger, right?!

23:32.605 --> 23:35.805
It's times like these that you can rely
on your new hero, Reiji Ozora!

23:36.475 --> 23:39.535
Next on Dragon Drive,
Promised Dive.

23:40.445 --> 23:41.915
You're asking if we're gonna be all right?

23:41.915 --> 23:43.285
Chibisuke, you're the one
who's gonna fight, you know.

23:43.285 --> 23:45.875
Promised Dive
Chibisuke, you're the one
who's gonna fight, you know.
